# `use boring.<module>` for an unrecognized module name must be a hard
# error in both `boring run` (this test) and `boring build` (tests/
# transpile.rs's registration) — unlike the generic filesystem `use` loader,
# which silently no-ops on a missing file (it assumes a native Rust module).
# `boring` is never a real crate, so there's no legitimate native fallback.
use boring.nope.*
print "should not reach"
